[[1024,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply for the two fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N12</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               arrives\ndirectly from the battery from the lines of the two maxifuses FAN1\nand FAN2 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : the fans operate when they receive an earth\ncommand.</p><p>The relays \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J32</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nspecific to the cooling system, receive supply to their coils from\nthe direct line (EFI) protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>They are energized by an earth signal coming\nfrom the engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>If the coolant temperature reaches the first\ntemperature stage, or the 4-stage pressure switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K10 (pin 3)\nindicates to control unit M10 - pin 42 of connector A - that the\nfirst pressure stage has been reached, control unit M10 sends an\nearth signal to 1st speed relay J30 from pin 90 of connector A,\nwhich energizes the coil.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               The relay then sends an earth which,\nvia the additional resistors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O12</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , operates\nboth fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N12</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which rotate at the first (slow)\nspeed.</p><p>If the engine coolant reaches a higher temperature\nlevel, or the 4 stage pressure switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K10 (pin 6) signals to\nthe control unit M10 - pin 81 of connector A - that a higher pressure\nlevel has been reached, then the control unit M10 sends an earth\nsignal, pin 69 of connector A,  to the two 2nd speed fan relays\nJ31 and J32 which energize the coils.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               The two relays then send\nan earth directly to the two fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N12</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which\nrotate at maximum speed.</p>"]]